 {"id":"nse-VHLTD-29-Jun-2026115319","type":"ipo","geo":"mumbai","city":"Mumbai","sector":"Consumer & Retail","imp":"lo","verified":true,"implication":"Rights issues under Indian securities law require SEBI approval of the Letter of Offer and compliance with ICDR (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations 2018; timeline from board approval to shareholder approval to SEBI clearance typically spans 3–6 months, and legal counsel must ensure statutory ratio thresholds and disclosure obligations are met.","framework":[{"ref":"SEBI (Issue of Capital and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2018 (ICDR), Regulation 74–93","note":"Central - governs rights issue process, including Letter of Offer content, statutory disclosures, timeline from approval to listing, and underwriting norms.","flag":"central"},{"ref":"Companies Act, 2013, Section 62","note":"Central - enables issuance of shares on a rights basis with prior shareholder approval by ordinary resolution or special resolution per Memorandum and Articles.","flag":"central"},{"ref":"Companies Act, 2013, Section 23","note":"Governs alteration of share capital, including increases via rights or other methods, and filing with Registrar of Companies (ROC).","flag":"central"},{"ref":"SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 (LODR), Regulation 30","note":"Mandates immediate disclosure of material events (board approval of rights issue) to stock exchanges.","flag":"central"},{"ref":"Companies Act, 2013, Section 192–198","note":"Governs convening of shareholder meetings (extraordinary general meeting for rights issue approval) including notice, quorum and voting thresholds.","flag":""},{"ref":"NSE Listing Rules and Bye-Laws","note":"NSE-specific continuous disclosure and filing requirements for listed companies undertaking capital raises.","flag":""},{"ref":"ICDR Regulations, 2018, Regulation 171–175","note":"Procedural rules for rights issue timeline, allotment, refund and crediting to Demat accounts.","flag":""}],"stage":"announced","value":"—","parties":"Viceroy Hotels Limited","time":"29 Jun 2026","headline":"Viceroy Hotels Limited announces rights issue of equity shares; Board approves Draft Letter of Offer","sum":"<b>Viceroy Hotels Limited's board has approved a rights issue of equity shares and constituted a Rights Issue Committee to oversee the offering.</b> The company approved the Draft Letter of Offer on 29 June 2026, signalling capital raise through preferential allocation to existing shareholders.","detail":"Viceroy Hotels Limited, a listed hospitality company on the National Stock Exchange, initiated a rights issue process via board resolution on 29 June 2026. The Board of Directors constituted a dedicated Rights Issue Committee to manage the issuance, and approved a Draft Letter of Offer-the foundational disclosure document required for regulatory submission to SEBI. Rights issues are commonly used by Indian companies to raise capital while preserving control structures and giving existing shareholders first right of refusal in proportion to their shareholding. The next regulatory milestone is SEBI approval of the Letter of Offer and shareholder approval at an extraordinary general meeting.","firms":[],"sources":[{"name":"NSE Corporate Archives - Viceroy Hotels Limited Outcome of Board Meeting","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/VICEROYHOTELSLTD_29062026115032_outcome.pdf","official":true,"blurb":"Official NSE disclosure of board meeting held 29 June 2026 approving rights issue of equity shares and constitution of Rights Issue Committee."},{"name":"BSE corporate announcements","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/corporates/ann.html","official":true,"blurb":"Official source - search by the parties to pull the primary filing/order."},{"name":"NSE corporate announcements","url":"https://www.nseindia.com/companies-listing/corporate-filings-announcements","official":true,"blurb":"Official source - search by the parties to pull the primary filing/order."},{"name":"SEBI public issues / DRHPs","url":"https://www.sebi.gov.in/filings/public-issues.html","official":true,"blurb":"Official source - search by the parties to pull the primary filing/order."}],"docs":[{"label":"NSE Outcome of Board Meeting - 29 June 2026","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/VICEROYHOTELSLTD_29062026115032_outcome.pdf"},{"label":"BSE corporate announcements","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/corporates/ann.html"},{"label":"NSE corporate announcements","url":"https://www.nseindia.com/companies-listing/corporate-filings-announcements"},{"label":"SEBI public issues / DRHPs","url":"https://www.sebi.gov.in/filings/public-issues.html"}],"timeline":[{"d":"29 Jun 2026","t":"Board of Directors meeting; approval of rights issue, constitution of Rights Issue Committee, and approval of Draft Letter of Offer."}],"score":21,"scoreReasons":["Corroborated by an official source","4 corroborating sources"],"enrichTier":"standard","structure":{"consideration":"—","conditions":["SEBI approval of Letter of Offer","Shareholder approval via extraordinary general meeting","Board constitution of Rights Issue Committee","Drafting and regulatory filing of Letter of Offer"],"approvals":["Board of Directors approval (29 Jun 2026)","Shareholder approval (pending)","SEBI approval (pending)"],"novel":"Standard rights issue mechanism; no novel structuring noted from disclosure.","triggers":[{"law":"SEBI ICDR Regulations 2018, Regulations 74–93","note":"Rights issue mandates full SEBI regulatory pathway including Letter of Offer review, disclosure compliance and post-allotment filing."},{"law":"Companies Act 2013, Section 62","note":"Requires prior shareholder approval by way of ordinary or special resolution; board has initiated via committee but shareholder vote still pending."},{"law":"SEBI LODR Regulations 2015, Regulation 30","note":"Immediate disclosure to NSE and BSE of board resolution approving rights issue and constitution of committee."}],"status":"Partly inferred"},"enrichedAt":"12 Aug 2026"},
 {"id":"nse-VIKRAMSOLR-29-Jun-2026172908","type":"ibc","geo":"other","city":"Chennai / National","sector":"Energy & Renewables","imp":"lo","verified":true,"implication":"Solar manufacturing sector insolvency triggers statutory 180-day CIRP timeline and mandatory creditor governance via Committee of Creditors (CoC); resolution plan must be voted and approved by CoC before NCLT confirmation, precedent for energy-sector distressed M&A and asset sales.","framework":[{"ref":"Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code, 2016 (IBC)","note":"Primary statute; Chapters II–IV govern CIRP, creditor governance, resolution plan approval and NCLT confirmation.","flag":"central"},{"ref":"IBC 2016, Section 5","note":"Definition of 'insolvency resolution process commencement date' and statutory timeline triggers.","flag":"central"},{"ref":"IBC 2016, Sections 21–32","note":"Resolution Professional appointment, duties, operational control, and Committee of Creditors formation and voting.","flag":"central"},{"ref":"IBC 2016, Section 30","note":"Resolution plan preparation and approval thresholds (66% CoC vote by voting share weighted by claims).","flag":"central"},{"ref":"IBBI (Insolvency Resolution Process for Corporate Persons) Regulations, 2016","note":"Procedural norms for CIRP conduct, timeline compliance, stakeholder communications, and RP governance.","flag":"central"},{"ref":"IBBI Code of Conduct Regulations, 2016","note":"Standards for RP professional conduct, conflict of interest, and fiduciary duties.","flag":""},{"ref":"Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements (LODR) Regulations, 2015 (SEBI)","note":"Exchange disclosure obligations for listed entity in insolvency; required intimations and investor updates.","flag":"central"},{"ref":"IBC 2016, Section 31 (as amended 2020)","note":"Persons excluded from submission or voting on resolution plans (promoters, related parties); amended framework.","flag":"amended"},{"ref":"IBC 2016, Section 12A (as inserted 2019)","note":"Fast-track CIRP and pre-packaged CIRP routes; timebound alternatives to standard 180-day process.","flag":"amended"}],"stage":"filed","value":"—","parties":"Vikram Solar Limited","time":"29 Jun 2026","headline":"Vikram Solar Limited enters Corporate Insolvency Resolution Process","sum":"<b>Vikram Solar Limited, a solar panel manufacturer, has been admitted into Corporate Insolvency Resolution Process (CIRP) under the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code, 2016.</b> The company informed NSE of the development via formal exchange intimation.","detail":"Vikram Solar Limited, a renewable energy equipment manufacturer, has entered into CIRP following a petition (by creditor or debtor self-admission). The company intimated NSE of the insolvency status via formal disclosure on 29 June 2026. Under IBC 2016, the company is now subject to a maximum 180-day resolution period (extendable by 90 days) during which a Resolution Professional (RP) will manage operations and oversee creditor-led restructuring or asset realisation. The admission order determines the insolvency estate and triggers suspension of promoter actions, freezing of related-party transactions, and commencement of claims process.","firms":[],"sources":[{"name":"NSE Intimation Filing","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/VSLCS_29062026172834_VSLINTIMATIONDTED29062026.pdf","official":true,"blurb":"Official NSE intimation by Vikram Solar Limited disclosing entry into CIRP; primary exchange disclosure dated 29 June 2026."},{"name":"BSE Corporate Announcements Database","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/investors/scriptinfo/corpannounce/","official":true,"blurb":"BSE listing exchange announcements page where Vikram Solar CIRP notice would be filed for dual-listed security."},{"name":"IBBI Official Website – Cases","url":"https://www.ibbi.gov.in/","official":true,"blurb":"Insolvency and Bankruptcy Board of India case registry; should contain registered Resolution Professional and case details for Vikram Solar CIRP."},{"name":"IBBI orders","url":"https://ibbi.gov.in/en/orders","official":true,"blurb":"Official source - search by the parties to pull the primary filing/order."},{"name":"NCLT orders","url":"https://nclt.gov.in/order-judgement-date-wise","official":true,"blurb":"Official source - search by the parties to pull the primary filing/order."}],"docs":[{"label":"NSE filing","url":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/VSLCS_29062026172834_VSLINTIMATIONDTED29062026.pdf"},{"label":"IBBI orders","url":"https://ibbi.gov.in/en/orders"},{"label":"NCLT orders","url":"https://nclt.gov.in/order-judgement-date-wise"}],"timeline":[{"d":"29 Jun 2026","t":"NSE intimation of CIRP status filed by Vikram Solar Limited"}],"score":21,"scoreReasons":["Corroborated by an official source","3 corroborating sources"],"enrichTier":"standard","structure":{"consideration":"—","conditions":["180-day CIRP period from admission order (extendable by further 90 days on CoC application)","All claims must be submitted to RP within prescribed period (typically 30 days from commencement notice)","CoC approval of resolution plan by 66% voting share majority (by claims value)","NCLT confirmation of resolution plan before implementation"],"approvals":["NCLT admission order (mandatory gateway)","Committee of Creditors formation and voting approval","NCLT final confirmation order for resolution plan"],"novel":"—","triggers":[{"law":"IBC 2016, Section 7/9/10","note":"Petition by operational creditor, financial creditor, or debtor self-admission; admission order triggered by NCLT finding of default."},{"law":"SEBI LODR Regulations 2015, Regulation 30","note":"Listed company must intimate exchange of insolvency status within prescribed timeline; material event affecting stock price and investor rights."},{"law":"IBC 2016, Section 5 & Schedule","note":"Commencement of insolvency triggers statutory clock; resolution window and creditor governance framework commence."}],"status":"Partly inferred"},"enrichedAt":"12 Aug 2026"}